          "title": "DBpedia 2015-10 | DBpedia - DBpedia – Linked Data Fragments",
          "url": "https://fragments.dbpedia.org/2015-10/en?object=%22Bill%20Brown%20is%20the%20Karla%20Scherer%20Distinguished%20Service%20Professor%20in%20American%20Culture%20at%20the%20University%20of%20Chicago%2C%20where%20he%20teaches%20in%20the%20Department%20of%20English%20Language%20and%20Literature%2C%20the%20Department%20of%20Visual%20Arts%2C%20and%20the%20College.%20He%20previously%20held%20the%20Edward%20Carson%20Waller%20Distinguished%20Service%20Professorship%20in%20Humanities%20and%20the%20George%20M.%20Pullman%20Professorship%2C%20and%20served%20as%20the%20chair%20of%20the%20University%27s%20English%20Language%20and%20Literature%20Department%20from%202006-2008.%20After%20a%20brief%20term%20as%20the%20Deputy%20Dean%20for%20Academic%20and%20Research%20Initiatives%20in%20the%20Division%20of%20the%20Humanities%2C%20Brown%20was%20recruited%20to%20be%20the%20new%20Deputy%20Provost%20for%20the%20Arts%20in%202014.%20As%20Deputy%20Provost%2C%20Brown%20oversees%20the%20programming%20and%20future%20of%20UChicago%20Arts%2C%20serves%20on%20the%20Arts%20Steering%20Committee%2C%20and%20chairs%20the%20UChicago%20Art%20Institutions%20subcommittee.%20He%20also%20serves%20on%20a%20number%20of%20other%20committees%20across%20campus%20-%20including%20the%20Executive%20Committee%20of%20the%20Karla%20Scherer%20Center%20for%20the%20Study%20of%20American%20Culture%20-%20and%20is%20the%20principal%20investigator%20for%20the%20Object%20Cultures%20Project%20at%20The%20Chicago%20Center%20for%20Contemporary%20Theory%20(3CT).%20He%20has%20co-edited%20the%20University%20of%20Chicago%27s%20peer-reviewed%20literary%20journal%2C%20Critical%20Inquiry%2C%20since%201993.Professor%20Brown%27s%20work%20focuses%20on%20American%20literature%2C%20with%20his%20second%20book%2C%20A%20Sense%20of%20Things%2C%20looking%20at%20the%20representation%20of%20objects%20in%2019th-century%20American%20literature.%20His%20interests%20have%20since%20progressed%20to%20modernism.%20He%20also%20has%20a%20long-standing%20interest%20in%20popular%20culture%2C%20and%20has%20written%20about%20Toy%20Story%20and%20Westerns%2C%20among%20other%20facets%20of%20American%20life.%20His%20major%20theoretical%20work%2C%20however%2C%20is%20on%20Thing%20theory%2C%20which%20borrows%20from%20Heidegger%27s%20object%2Fthing%20distinction%20to%20look%20at%20the%20role%20of%20objects%20that%20have%20become%20manifest%20in%20a%20way%20that%20sets%20them%20apart%20from%20the%20world%20in%20which%20they%20exist.%20He%20edited%20a%20special%20issue%20of%20Critical%20Inquiry%20on%20this%20subject%2C%20which%20won%20the%20CELJ%20award%20for%20Best%20Special%20Issue%20of%20an%20academic%20journal%20in%202002.%20His%20essay%2C%20%22The%20Dark%20Wood%20of%20Postmodernity%3A%20Space%2C%20Faith%2C%20Allegory%2C%22%20which%20treats%20religious%20themes%20in%20the%20work%20of%20Marxian%20cultural%20theorist%20Frederic%20Jameson%20and%20in%20postmodern%20culture%20generally%2C%20was%20awarded%20the%20Modern%20Language%20Association%27s%20William%20Riley%20Parker%20Prize%20in%202005.Brown%20has%20a%20B.A.%20from%20Duke%20University%2C%20an%20M.A.%20in%20Creative%20Writing%20(poetry)%20from%20Stanford%20University%2C%20and%20a%20Ph.D.%20from%20Stanford%20University%27s%20Modern%20Thought%20and%20Literature%20program.%20He%20has%20been%20teaching%20at%20the%20University%20of%20Chicago%20since%201989.%22%40en#1"
